WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
In The Purge: Election Year, Joe’s Deli&nbsp;
serves as a symbol of The American Dream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.480
for Joe and his community, but some of&nbsp;
the images seen around the store have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.400
greater significance than you might have realized.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.640
Election Year shows us the height of a revolution&nbsp;
staged by the lower class against the government.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.720
This is essentially the New Civil Rights Movement&nbsp;
of the United States. In the world of The Purge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.640
the poor are discriminated against. Not only can&nbsp;
the wealthy better afford to protect themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.080
during The Purge, but if you read into the&nbsp;
lore detailed on the New Founders website,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.320
you’ll see they’ve enacted laws like the Contributing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.240
Citizens Provision of 2019 that straight&nbsp;
up allows discrimination against the poor.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.600
There are both subtle and not so&nbsp;
subtle comparisons to the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.040
Civil Rights Movement that took place&nbsp;
in the United States 86 years prior.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.040
Joe’s Deli is his pride and joy, his little&nbsp;
piece of the pie, as he puts it. For him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.000
the American Dream means owning and&nbsp;
operating his own business that serves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.560
the community, but his dream, like the dream of&nbsp;
his ancestor, Martin Luther King Jr., is crushed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.240
when his insurance company intentionally&nbsp;
raises his rates 1 day before The Purge.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.200
“They just raised the premium on my Purge&nbsp;
coverage. By thousands. The day before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.680
damn Purge. If I don’t pay it by tomorrow&nbsp;
I have no Purge coverage for this store.”

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.040
In previous Purge movies, we’ve learned&nbsp;
that weapon and home security companies are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.880
the most likely shills for the political&nbsp;
party that created The Purge, the NFFA,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.000
and Election Year suggests that insurance&nbsp;
companies have joined that category.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.920
But some of the images seen in and around the&nbsp;
deli are more than just a generic symbol of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.360
civil rights -- they reference specific&nbsp;
historical events that foreshadow what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.800
happens at the end of the movie. There&nbsp;
are also more modern references, in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.560
Election Year may have actually predicted&nbsp;
some future events, so stick around to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.480
end of this video to hear about all of&nbsp;
it. This video is sponsored by Audible.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:41.200
I hereby proclaim, that all men shall subscribe&nbsp;
to CZsWorld and ring the deathbell for all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:46.080
notifications! Welcome to Things You Missed.&nbsp;
If you’ve been waiting for a video where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.480
Emo Abraham Lincoln, regular Abraham Lincoln&nbsp;
and Angry Abraham Lincoln all collide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.440
this is the episode for you. If you&nbsp;
want to hear about the hidden meanings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.560
encoded in the third Purge movie,&nbsp;
you are also in the right place.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.920
This would be the last installment&nbsp;
directed by series creator James Demonaco,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:03.920
although he would stay on as screenwriter going&nbsp;
forward. If you look at Election Year literally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.160
it looks like the silliest, most ridiculous entry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:10.000
but we can find deeper meaning when looking&nbsp;
on a metaphorical level. Let’s get into it.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.600
All around Washington DC, there&nbsp;
are NFFA logos and advertisements,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.840
but in low-income areas like the area near the&nbsp;
freeway underpass and right around the deli, we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.400
see that the banners have been defaced, a symbol&nbsp;
of the tension that exists between the social classes.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.960
The divide between the rich and&nbsp;
poor is highlighted by the use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.880
of technology. The movie is set in 2040,&nbsp;
so you’d expect some futuristic gadgets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.800
like Leo’s remote detonating briefcase&nbsp;
and GPS tracking bullets, but Joe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.840
Marcos and Lainey use devices that feel outdated&nbsp;
even today. From standard definition monitors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:49.840
to broken grandpa clocks to Samsung&nbsp;
Galaxy S2’s and even this monstrosity.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.520
As I mentioned, the deli is decorated with&nbsp;
photos of the most prominent figures of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.440
original American Civil Rights Movement, like&nbsp;
Malcolm X, who was an advocate of African American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:02.642
human rights in the 1960s who was criticized&nbsp;
for refusing to denounce violence as a form of self-defense.

00:03:02.642 --> 00:03:08.151
INTERVIEWER: "So Martin is your friend, yet you would disagree to his approach to what he wants to accomplish?"

00:03:08.151 --> 00:03:13.310
X: "Definitely, if his approach would bring about what the black man in America needs, 

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:17.434
to completely eliminate the problem that we have, I would say well and good."

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:21.200
The Purge: Election Year has its own Malcolm&nbsp;
X -- it’s Dante Bishop, the homeless man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:25.280
turned revolutionary fighter who planned to&nbsp;
assassinate the NFFA’s presidential candidate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.823
The independent candidate Charlie&nbsp;
Roan criticizes him on his methods.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:36.266
“Mr. Bishop, I’ve heard stories of&nbsp;
tactics that you employ on Purge night.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.880
I can’t say that I agree with any of it.”

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.880
Bishop&nbsp;
changes his ways in the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.680
but they do share the same fate&nbsp;
of being taken out by extremists.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:47.520
Another picture seen in the deli is of Harriet&nbsp;
Tubman. Harriet was born into slavery in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:51.440
1820s, and her most notable accomplishment&nbsp;
was operating the Underground Railroad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.840
a network of secret routes&nbsp;
and safehouses designed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.640
help escort African Americans&nbsp;
out of slavery in the south.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.520
The new Civil Rights Movement isn’t&nbsp;
about slavery and race though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.120
it’s about money and homelessness, so&nbsp;
the new Harriet Tubman is Laney Rucker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:06.800
who spends her Purge night working in a triage&nbsp;
van to help Purge victims get to underground&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.000
safehouses throughout the city where they&nbsp;
can hide out and get medical attention.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.560
Tubman also worked as nurse during the American&nbsp;
Civil War and notably led a military operation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:19.760
known as the Raid on Combahee Ferry where 750&nbsp;
people were rescued from slavery on Union ships.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:24.080
At one point, Laney’s character is implied to also&nbsp;
have some kind of notable military background,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.496
but it’s never explained or expanded upon&nbsp;
and isn’t relevant to the story in any way.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:30.960
“That’s Laney Rucker, Kimmy.”&nbsp;

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:41.760
“Laney Rucker? They called you Pequeña Muerte.&nbsp;
Little Death. You’re my motherf***ing hero.”

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:45.280
This detail seems to only exist to&nbsp;
explain how she knows how to use a gun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.760
or as an added parallel to Harriet Tubman.
Then there’s Frederick Douglass. Like the others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:53.680
he was an important figure in slavery abolition&nbsp;
and Civil Rights. He went on to hold several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:57.280
political offices and at one point he was&nbsp;
nominated to become Vice President of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.120
United States. If he does have a counterpart&nbsp;
in the movie, I’m guessing it’s Senator Roan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:05.040
but there may also be another historical figure&nbsp;
who serves as a stronger reflection of Roan.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:10.080
The most recognizable person pictured here, the&nbsp;
true Patriot of his time, was Tom Brady; this was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.920
before he became a Buccaneer, but other than that,&nbsp;
there’s Martin Luther King Jr., who of course is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:18.000
the most prolific Civil Rights speaker of all&nbsp;
time, with his famous I Have a Dream Speech.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.720
There are a couple of pictures of him&nbsp;
in the deli, but I want to look at this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.880
one in particular, which was taken at a&nbsp;
press conference on November 5th, 1964,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:28.640
just after Lyndon B Johnson was elected&nbsp;
as President. Johnson was known for his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:32.880
domestic policies known as the “Great Society”&nbsp;
program and the “War on Poverty” program,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:37.200
which assisted millions of families out of poverty&nbsp;
during his administration. Senator Roan’s platform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.360
is all about helping out low-income people,&nbsp;
primarily by promising to end The Purge.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.640
The day this photo was taken, Johnson&nbsp;
spoke with King Jr. to thank him for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:47.680
his support and ask him to get&nbsp;
behind the poverty initiative.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.920
“We’re gonna spend a lot of time with Schrieber&nbsp;
on our poverty thing, I wish you’d give a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:56.320
thought to it, because that offers a lot&nbsp;
of opportunity for our young people.”&nbsp;

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:00.240
“Well, good, good, and again,&nbsp;
let me congratulate you.”

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.640
So as you can see there are a lot of similarities&nbsp;
between Senator Roan and Lyndon B Johnson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:08.880
but there may be one more parallel in looking&nbsp;
at the circumstances of when they took office.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.640
Johnson was elected shortly after becoming&nbsp;
President due to the assassination of John&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:16.560
F Kennedy, while Roan was elected shortly&nbsp;
after the assassination of Caleb Warrens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.600
the NFFA leader that gets sniped&nbsp;
down at the end of the movie.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.800
The main characters would not be the&nbsp;
only ones who represent a person or group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:27.280
of historical significance, and there are&nbsp;
many other secrets waiting to be uncovered.

