00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.400
The previous film, The Purge: Anarchy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:46.400
started to explore how the NFFA was creating&nbsp;
a religious aspect to the Purge as part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:50.240
their wider effort to manipulate people into&nbsp;
participating. Here, it’s front and center,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:54.320
as the new NFFA Presidential candidate is&nbsp;
a minister who holds a midnight ceremony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:58.080
on Purge night where less fortunate people&nbsp;
and political enemies are to be sacrificed.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.840
There are many moments that build up to the finale&nbsp;
at the cathedral, from the first shot of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:06.000
evening showing the sun setting behind a building&nbsp;
that looks like a church to a church being the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:10.880
only location labeled on the GPS system that&nbsp;
the NFFA’s mercenaries use to track the Senator.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.720
The United States has something called an&nbsp;
Establishment Clause, the separation of church&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:18.720
and state, but we see that all of the New Founding&nbsp;
Fathers are the religious leaders, serving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:22.960
as ministers and priests. This isn’t a separate&nbsp;
religion that they happen to be a part of, this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:28.000
clearly an NFFA event, Minister Owens even admits&nbsp;
that Midnight Purge Mass belongs to his party.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:32.320
His first name is Edwidge, a french name&nbsp;
meaning “war”. He is a minister of war,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:35.680
and as Senator Roan suggests in a&nbsp;
debate, murder is his new religion.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:39.520
He’s joined at the altar by Harmon&nbsp;
James. Harmon is also a French name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:42.880
meaning soldier, and he’s the one seen&nbsp;
carrying out the ceremonious purging.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:46.640
On the topic of nomenclature, there are a couple&nbsp;
of notable names on the other side as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:50.720
As I mentioned in his Horror History episode,&nbsp;
Dante Bishop is given a name for the first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:55.520
in this movie, previously only being referred to&nbsp;
as a stranger. Dante refers to Dante’s Inferno,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:59.680
a famous 14th century poem about the journey&nbsp;
through hell, while his surname Bishop would refer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:04.000
to the clergy member in the Christian church.&nbsp;
So his name comes off as an oxymoron. Perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.920
he’s split somewhere between heaven and hell.&nbsp;
He has good intentions and wants to help people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:12.640
but uses violent tactics to make his points. At&nbsp;
the end he has to choose between sin and virtue.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.160
Also of note, he has a right hand man whose&nbsp;
name is Angel. Earlier on the streets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.769
a crazy purger on chants about the gates of hell.

00:09:19.105 --> 00:09:24.437
“That’s right! The gates of hell&nbsp;
will open and invite me in!”

00:09:24.437 --> 00:09:27.120
The movie seems to be showing us&nbsp;
the contrast between traditional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.080
religious beliefs where behaviour would&nbsp;
dictate going to heaven or hell and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:33.760
NFFA’s new distorted religious&nbsp;
system where sin is glorified.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:37.840
One name that we’ve seen come up in every&nbsp;
Purge movie is Sabian. Arlo Sabian was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:41.520
NFFA Chief of Staff in The First Purge,&nbsp;
Mr. Sabian was a neighbor in the Purge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:46.080
and diner patron in The Purge: Anarchy and&nbsp;
now Mrs. Sabian is a customer at Joe’s Deli.

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:48.880
“Mrs. Sabian, I wish I knew.”

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:52.640
The name Sabian is a staple in every&nbsp;
movie made by director James Demonaco,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:55.840
as is Staten Island -- you can spot&nbsp;
some channel 11 Purge coverage of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:58.800
Staten Island on the TV in the&nbsp;
back of the Senator’s living room.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:02.640
And speaking of stuff that appears in other Purge&nbsp;
movies, were we not supposed to notice when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:07.280
sirens sound, they just ripped an unused shot from&nbsp;
The Purge: Anarchy? This is clearly LA. My only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:10.640
guess is maybe they were trying to encompass how&nbsp;
far the Purge series has come with this sequence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:13.840
which starts in the Senator’s home, (the&nbsp;
first movie takes place all inside one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:18.080
home) then showing Los Angeles (where the second&nbsp;
movie takes place) then showing Washington DC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:20.880
which is the capital, it’s&nbsp;
representative of the entire country.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:23.760
There’s also a connection to the&nbsp;
original film in that the flashback&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:27.040
of Roan’s family being purged takes&nbsp;
place on the same night as that movie.

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:30.720
Before the NFFA hired mercenaries invade&nbsp;
her home, there are a few significant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:34.240
items I noticed upstairs, like these two&nbsp;
crane ornaments. In Japanese culture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:38.240
cranes are said to represent good fortune and&nbsp;
longevity, two traits that seem appropriate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:41.760
for Barnes and Roan who survive until&nbsp;
the next morning against all odds.

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:43.760
There’s also a turtle on the Senator’s mantle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:47.280
a Chinese symbol for longevity. This&nbsp;
is seen just before Leo bursts into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:51.360
room and has her put on a bulletproof vest,&nbsp;
her metaphorical turtle shell, if you will.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.080
Leo and Roan escape just before&nbsp;
the bad guys break into the room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:57.760
and their leader unmasks himself, revealing&nbsp;
his affiliation with many of the most evil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:00.800
groups throughout history. We’ve gotta&nbsp;
slow it down to understand all of them.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.320
The more well known ones are the Nazi symbol,&nbsp;
the party responsible for the Holocaust,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:07.760
the Ku Klux Klan, a white supremecist&nbsp;
group, and the confederate flag of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:10.800
the breakaway state that fought for&nbsp;
slavery in the American Civil War.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:15.680
He also has a tattoo that says 88, which is&nbsp;
supposedly a numerical code. H is the 8th letter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:20.640
of the alphabet, so this translates to HH which&nbsp;
stands for Heil Hitler. Another tattoo says AB,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:24.880
an acronym for Aryan Brotherhood, a neo-Nazi&nbsp;
prison gang and organized crime syndicate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:29.280
My Google Search history feels very dirty after&nbsp;
looking this stuff up and that’s coming from me.

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:32.000
My favorite search result though, was&nbsp;
when I looked up what a spider web&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.360
tattoo on one’s head signifies,&nbsp;
and found the answer: a serious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:39.280
lapse in judgement. Upon looking further&nbsp;
I found out it meant they were in prison.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:42.080
The assault rifle on his temple&nbsp;
signifies that he’s a gun carrier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:46.320
and the words Free in America are written&nbsp;
across his face. Which isn’t a bad message by itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:48.560
but it takes a darker meaning&nbsp;
in the world of The Purge.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.840
On the back of his head he has the American&nbsp;
Eagle. I’m guessing it’s not because he’s a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:55.600
fan of the clothing brand… or the roller&nbsp;
coaster, although he does seem to like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:59.600
Spiderwebs. There’s also an American flag,&nbsp;
almost as if the US has become the newest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:03.120
evil group in this universe. We see that&nbsp;
the country definitely attracts negative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:07.360
attention when a story on the news tells about&nbsp;
the latest travel trend called murder tourism.

00:12:08.852 --> 00:12:10.880
“We’re here to experience the purge. To&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:14.880
k*ll. Release all the anger&nbsp;
and h*te. Be like Americans.”

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:18.400
I think this is kind of a commentary on&nbsp;
how other countries see America today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:22.000
where the rate of mass shootings is much&nbsp;
higher than any other developed country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:25.680
Of course, I’m American, so I can only&nbsp;
assume how other countries see us.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:29.120
There are also several examples of&nbsp;
medieval weapons like a guillotine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.280
a pendulum and a mace being used to purge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:34.960
which I see as a symbol for the primitive&nbsp;
nature of weapon regulations in the US.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:38.880
The murder tourists play an interesting role&nbsp;
later in the story, as Barnes is trying to escort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:42.880
Senator Roan to safety and they’re stalked by a&nbsp;
drone, which we later find out to be a Russain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:47.520
drone. In other words, this American politician&nbsp;
is being followed around by Russian spies.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:51.840
The Purge: Election Year was released in 2016,&nbsp;
which was an election year in real life for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:55.680
United States. It is said that Russia tried&nbsp;
to influence the results of that election by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.680 --> 00:13:00.640
creating bots on social media websites to spread&nbsp;
propaganda. The drone is literally a Russian bot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:05.200
and when Leo shoots it down, the explosion lights&nbsp;
up a mural that says Keep Washington Beautiful.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:07.520
If it’s intentional, it’s an interesting metaphor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:11.280
I’ll just let you decide how intentional it&nbsp;
really is though. The movie came out in July,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:14.800
but the election didn’t begin until the end&nbsp;
of the year. It’s hard to say when the Russain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:19.120
initiative would have begun, seeing as how&nbsp;
I’m not a member of the CIA or FBI. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:23.520
paranoia of Russian plants has been a concept&nbsp;
in American culture that goes back for decades.

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:27.040
That being said, the next scene does&nbsp;
seem to predict a Russian collusion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:30.960
where bot accounts on social media pretending&nbsp;
to be American citizens would spread information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:34.000
that might influence the election.&nbsp;
In The Purge, we have these Russian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:39.040
tourists masquerading around in Washington DC&nbsp;
in the costumes of typical American icons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:43.200
and they almost quite literally influence the&nbsp;
election by purging one of the candidates.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:47.760
So we’ve discussed how many characters and groups&nbsp;
have historical or societal significance in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:52.160
story. What about Kimmy and her Purge gang? We&nbsp;
first meet her trying to steal candy from Joe’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:56.720
Deli, then even when confronted about it, she’s&nbsp;
resistant to give it up. Kimmy represents greed.

00:13:56.720 --> 00:14:00.480
She comes back during The Purge with the&nbsp;
intention of stealing back the candy bar.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:04.160
“I want my candy bar. And I’m gonna take it.”

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:08.080
When she returns, we see that she’s already&nbsp;
got it all: nice cars decorated with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:12.240
bright lights, bejeweled guns made of&nbsp;
solid gold and flashy costumes because…

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:15.040
“THE PURGE IS HALLOWEEN FOR ADULTS!”

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:20.160
No, Halloween as an adult is Halloween for adults.&nbsp;
I appreciate the positive energy though dude.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:24.000
Kimmy and her gang are basically the typical&nbsp;
American millennial archetype. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:26.960
this movie is set in 2040, so&nbsp;
they aren’t actual millennials;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:30.720
this is just another social commentary on&nbsp;
our own time period. She isn’t willing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:33.840
buy the candy bar because she just&nbsp;
feels she has the right to take it.

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:37.940
[clip]

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:43.600
Her greed isn’t limited to material things&nbsp;
either, she’s also a massive attention freak.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:47.680
Notice how their crew isn’t dressed for stealth&nbsp;
combat like most purgers. They deck their cars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:52.880
out with lights and blast loud music, they wear skimpy&nbsp;
outfits and wear mascots costumes and anime masks.

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:55.440
For them, Purge is all about&nbsp;
being the center of attention,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:59.280
taking whatever they want and taking out&nbsp;
anyone who tries to stop them. Her crew is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:03.200
so self absorbed that they don’t even hear&nbsp;
Laney’s van driving up to take them out.

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:11.040
This is actually one of many just…&nbsp;
kind of dumb moments in this movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:13.600
Like when Leo and the Senator&nbsp;
encounter the swinging pendulum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:17.440
and they try to time it when there’s clearly&nbsp;
just plenty of room for them to crawl underneath.

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:20.000
I feel like I’m willing to forgive&nbsp;
some of the ridiculousness though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:23.200
because this entry does have probably&nbsp;
my favorite line in the franchise:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:31.120
“We are going to use this year’s Purge&nbsp;
to do some Spring Cleaning gentlemen…”

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:37.280
The next Purge installment would be the&nbsp;
poorly titled prequel, The First Purge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:40.560
which I’ve already covered here on Things&nbsp;
You Missed when it came out in 2018, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:44.560
it really doesn’t hold up. Like I need to redo the&nbsp;
video and make it good this time. I would always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:48.240
try to do these episodes when the movie was in&nbsp;
theaters to capitalize on the hype, but now that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:52.320
movies aren’t in theaters, I realize I can make&nbsp;
a much better episode if I take my time with it.

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:57.120
So join me in the next Things You Missed as we&nbsp;
revisit The First Purge. Remember to subscribe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.120 --> 00:16:01.920
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, RING&nbsp;
the deathbell and select ALL notifications,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:07.200
and I will see you in the next one. Assuming we&nbsp;
both survive. If you don’t want to get purged,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:10.926
stay home, wear a mask if you go out&nbsp;
for essentials. You know the drill.

